Adreno650 01db67e0 tests: SMMU register peers accept TLBIVAL (64-bit) and nothing else 64-bit

The fork merged UniXNU/ArmSmmu4K main (6d4441d), whose live update drops a small unmap page by page:
ArmSmmu4KLiveUpdateContextBatch -> update() -> ArmSmmu4KSyncContextTlbPages -> 64-bit write of TLBIVAL at
context bank + 0x620 (traced with gdb in a host build: NativeAdrenoVm::unmap, at = 0x22620). The fork's tests
were not updated with that merge: their peers still CHECK(0) on any 64-bit write, so test_gmumap and test_vm stop
at the first unmap. Upstream Adreno740 (122a8f1) changed the same peers to store 64-bit writes. These peers are
stricter than upstream: a 64-bit write is accepted only at +0x620 of a context bank (offset >= 0x20000).

Test fixture only; no driver source changes. Applied by scripts/test_adreno650.py (patches/adreno650/series).
